  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c9496aff-c93c-4ae1-a339-e98cc86624e5",
    "name": "ALTR Management Setup Guide API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Welcome to the Swagger documentation for ALTR's Management API (MAPI). MAPI allows ALTR customers to configure data sources and governance policy within the ALTR platform and is used to power ALTR's own UI. ALTR Enterprise customers are able to use MAPI to automate the configuration of data sources and governance policy.\n\nMAPI does not include the endpoints for ALTR's tokenization API; documentation on ALTR's tokenization API can be found [here](https://docs.altr.com/reference).\n\nMAPI uses [HTTP Basic Authentication](https://swagger.io/docs/specification/authentication/basic-authentication/). MAPI credentials can be obtained on the [API page](https://altrnet.live.altr.com/settings/preferences/api) (found under Settings > Preferences > API) of ALTR's portal for Enterprise and Enterprise + customers. Usernames are the 'Key Names' listed on that page, and Passwords are the 'Key Secret' provided when an API key is created.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Support\n Email: support@altr.com",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
